Why this licence: the sheets in derivations/ restate text from Wikipedia,
which is CC BY-SA 4.0, and its ShareAlike term requires adaptations to carry
the same licence. Some sheets also restate Gyubeom Im, "Notes on Kalman
Filter (KF, EKF, ESKF, IEKF, IESKF)" (arXiv:2406.06427, CC BY 4.0), which
permits this. Every sheet names its sources; see ../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
The rest of this directory -- the canon, its edges, seeds and notation -- is
original and is placed under the same licence so that one rule covers all
the content.

Exception: library_code.json holds excerpts of robot_localization, which
remain under that project's BSD 3-Clause licence. Each excerpted file's full
copyright notice, conditions and disclaimer are kept in the file's "notices"
field and must travel with the excerpts.

The code that produces and reads this content is licensed under MIT; see
../LICENSE.
